      "worked_solution": "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-2z+13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨5,0,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2y-3z-25=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨5,0,-2⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+15j+10k \\\\  & =⟨4,15,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
